{
  "summary": "This experiment tested transformer aggregation in place of avgpool on the RNA-only, multiprofile, PCA-2000 branch, changing only the aggregation strategy relative to llm_summary_003 to isolate its effect. Validation accuracy dropped to ~0.519 (F1: ~0.480) from ~0.591 (F1: ~0.573) under avgpool, indicating that in this clean single-variable comparison, transformer aggregation underperformed simple averaging by approximately 0.07 in accuracy. It remains uncertain whether this gap generalizes to multimodal configurations where transformer aggregation might better handle heterogeneous feature distributions, or whether the observed underperformance reflects a limitation of the transformer architecture under the current data regime rather than a fundamental disadvantage of attention-based aggregation."
}

